  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate $F(3)$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{2}^{x}(3{t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t.$",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(3)={\\int }_{2}^{3}(3{t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(3{t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+{t}^{2})\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =({3}^{3}+{3}^{2})-({2}^{3}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =(27+9)-(8+4) \\\\  & =36-12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
